2026-04-02 23:55:56 - Agent_20260402235253 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 10 CodeQL queries across the Jenkins Script Security plugin focusing on Groovy script execution flows. Key findings:

1. TRUE POSITIVE (line 443): When sandbox=true, user-controlled script content flows directly to GroovyShell.runScript() WITHOUT hash-based administrator approval. The only protection is the Groovy sandbox interceptor. Historical sandbox escape vulnerabilities (CVE-2019-1003000, etc.) demonstrate this is a real attack surface.

2. FALSE POSITIVE (line 450): Non-sandbox path - script flows to sh.evaluate() but is properly gated by ScriptApproval.using() which verifies the script hash against the admin-approved list and throws UnapprovedUsageException if not found.

3. FALSE POSITIVE (SystemCommandLanguage line 40): ExtensionList registry lookup, not a command execution point.

4. FALSE POSITIVE (ScriptApproval.configuring() line 615): Script registration/approval management method, not an execution point.

5. FALSE POSITIVE (ScriptApproval.using() if-statements lines 627/633): These are the actual approval enforcement guards (empty-script special case and throw-if-unapproved), not bypasses.

6. FALSE POSITIVE (GroovyShell instantiation line 436): Shell uses SecureCompilerConfiguration and is executed within GroovySandbox.runScript() scope which applies the sandbox interceptor properly.

Total: 1 true positive, 5 false positives submitted.
