Query 1 (7 findings in ScriptApproval.java):
- configuring() at line 590: Auto-approves scripts for admins - intentional design with explicit Jenkins.ADMINISTER permission check
- configuring() at line 615 (deprecated): Delegates with approveIfAdmin=false - more restrictive, not a vulnerability
- using() at line 626: Security enforcement gate that throws UnapprovedUsageException - not a vulnerability
- configuring(ClasspathEntry) at line 652: Admin auto-approval for classpath entries - intentional with ADMINISTER check
- using(ClasspathEntry) at line 724: Security enforcement gate that throws UnapprovedClasspathException - not a vulnerability
- approveScript() at line 964: Admin-only AJAX method with explicit checkPermission(ADMINISTER) + CSRF protection via @JavaScriptMethod
- denyScript() at line 982: Admin-only AJAX method with explicit checkPermission(ADMINISTER) + CSRF protection

