- sh.evaluate() at line 450: Admin-approved script flows to GroovyShell execution - intentional design where Jenkins admins are trusted to run arbitrary Groovy code. The using() call serves as the enforcement gate.

The core analysis: Jenkins admins are explicitly trusted to execute arbitrary code on the controller - this is the documented Jenkins security model. The Script Security plugin is designed to protect against non-admin script execution, not to restrict admin capabilities. All auto-approval paths require Jenkins.ADMINISTER permission, which is not exploitable by unprivileged users.
